Recently, I was able to attend a play by the name of  Why Women Trip by Torie in Dallas Texas. The Play featured Momma Dee from Love &amp; Hip Hop Atlanta, Benét Embry (Host of The Benet Embry Show) KayDee Carr, Lucretia Johnson, Reggie French (Host of R&amp;R and That D Radio Show), Ronald Clemons, Mia Hunt, (Irma P. Hall Award Winner) Sherry Hurnes, Zebretta Johnson and Steven Lewis. The Play is directed by Award winning actor, director, and musician Snoop Robinson.

<span class="rephrase-phrase ng-scope"><span class="text ng-binding ng-scope">The stage play is based on true life events about a lady named Shari Johnson.</span></span><span class="rephrase-phrase ng-scope"><span class="text ng-binding ng-scope"> The story showcases how quickly love can turn into hatred.</span></span><span class="rephrase-phrase ng-scope"><span class="text ng-binding ng-scope"> Shari meets and falls in love with the passion of her life Dorian Brooks.  The love connection between two went into a whirlwind and plan on living together forever.  </span></span>

<img class="aligncenter wp-image-943 size-full" src="http://35.224.26.164/wp-content/uploads/2017/08/IMG_2239-e1502124020230.jpg" alt="" width="2448" height="3264" />

The special guests included Internet sensation Irvin "Mr. Steal Ya Grandma" Randle and Music By Silk member Lil G. The play was really hilarious and is definitely something that I would go see again.  Special thanks to Torie Lee and Snoop Robinson for the invite.

